        "Performance Features",
        "1. Large air intake and low energy consumption.\n2. Capable of self‑air‑suction and self‑pulp‑suction. Adopts horizontal layout and requires no froth pump.\n3. Low impeller peripheral speed and long service life of wearing parts. Especially, the service life of impeller and stator is more than doubled compared with similar flotation machines.\n4. The clearance between impeller and stator is relatively large. The increase of clearance caused by wear has little influence on air intake capacity.\n5. The pulp inside the cell realizes vertical double‑circulation in a fixed flow pattern, which is favorable for the suspension of coarse‑grained minerals\n",
